ed":null},"corridor":{"origin_site_id":"48_201_0069","half_width_deg":22.5,"max_km":15.0,"wind_from_deg":[227.0,114.0]},"packet":{"draft_en":"On May 27, 2024, the Texas state monitor at Houston Milby Park recorded 14.28 ppb of 1,3-butadiene in the 3:00 p.m. CST hour, against a 7-day median of 0.67 ppb. Wind there came from 114 degrees at 4.5 mph. The wind was too light to trace where the air came from, so no upwind corridor is drawn. No matching report was found in the records checked; the search is incomplete. Requested follow-up: confirm whether any facility in this corridor reported a release that hour.","draft_es":"El 27 de mayo de 2024, el monitor estatal de Texas en Houston Milby Park registró 14.28 ppb de 1,3-butadieno en la hora de las 3:00 p. m. CST, frente a una mediana de 7 días de 0.67 ppb. El viento venía de 114 grados a 4.5 mph. El viento era demasiado débil para saber de dónde venía el aire, así que no se traza un corredor. No se encontró un informe correspondiente en los registros revisados; la búsqueda está incompleta. Seguimiento solicitado: confirmar si alguna instalación en este corredor reportó una emisión a esa hora.","drafted_by":"template (deterministic, no AI)","guard":{"passed":true,"rejected":[]}},"cannot_say":["A matching report is not proof the facility caused every reading; other sources can add to a spike.","'Not yet reported' is not a finding about any facility: Texas requires a report only at or above a reportable quantity, and air readings cannot measure how much was released (30 TAC 101.201).","The upwind corridor comes from wind direction at one monitor (geometry only), not a dispersion model; it cannot tell facilities along the same bearing apart.","Facility coordinates are as published by EPA ECHO and may be approximate.","Only regulator-grade monitors whose data the state publishes are used (including two industry-funded Houston Regional Monitoring sites), never low-cost sensors."],"provenance":[{"file":"backtest/agc_2024_48_20